[{:db/id 17592186059754 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ccf4f432-0d42-54bc-b36a-bd39fd754033"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059563 :question/problem "Find the inverse of ![](images/89/8967a472cff03599b1c2c94704fc9dc7272dc2a344d1876309dce1010a7ecc1f.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(8-12)+2(-3-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 14 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n![](images/51/51ba8948d60b649bea88218e86b2ea39cbecfe8014367a3def09d2aeb7667460.svg)\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/b6/b6339df9152864283a9ed0b938c2183da94121edec8d5b434566b2953e5bd0b0.svg)\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{9}{2} & 7 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & -2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059565 :question/problem "Determine the entry $a'_{23}$ in the inverse of the matrix ![](images/96/967f00655054db75990de13f3634f8d0b320ffde849057ce8cc9a19c58754aa2.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059755 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-60094f6c-d2bd-58df-8627-15176f255263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059564 :question/problem "The entry $a'_{31}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n![](images/4b/4b816f3bc511cd6170658d9b75715fc6385feeea1e768cd44d1bd199b67bf853.svg) \nequals $1$. Find the value of $k$." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ccf4f432-0d42-54bc-b36a-bd39fd754033" :question/id #uuid "ccf4f432-0d42-54bc-b36a-bd39fd754033" :question/math-academy-id "q-73478" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4b1f25d6-5390-5fe3-998f-b7a40d9649c3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b1f25d6-5390-5fe3-998f-b7a40d9649c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b1f25d6-5390-5fe3-998f-b7a40d9649c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-39a3852a-5680-51e4-9e2a-405e8aa0a909" :answer-field/choices ["answer-95310ad0-4ea0-549a-b41e-47e2e1481ffb" "answer-39a3852a-5680-51e4-9e2a-405e8aa0a909" "answer-fc2f21f0-c001-5a27-883c-872065513e5c" "answer-b9fbec83-d0b7-55ad-a7b0-15c8c1d2d21d" "answer-16cc7665-faef-5318-96fb-c89a1b7adc64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95310ad0-4ea0-549a-b41e-47e2e1481ffb" :answer/id #uuid "95310ad0-4ea0-549a-b41e-47e2e1481ffb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39a3852a-5680-51e4-9e2a-405e8aa0a909" :answer/id #uuid "39a3852a-5680-51e4-9e2a-405e8aa0a909" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc2f21f0-c001-5a27-883c-872065513e5c" :answer/id #uuid "fc2f21f0-c001-5a27-883c-872065513e5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9fbec83-d0b7-55ad-a7b0-15c8c1d2d21d" :answer/id #uuid "b9fbec83-d0b7-55ad-a7b0-15c8c1d2d21d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16cc7665-faef-5318-96fb-c89a1b7adc64" :answer/id #uuid "16cc7665-faef-5318-96fb-c89a1b7adc64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-60094f6c-d2bd-58df-8627-15176f255263" :question/id #uuid "60094f6c-d2bd-58df-8627-15176f255263" :question/math-academy-id "q-104435" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $2.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-k-6)-0+1(6-k) \\\\  & =-k-6+6-k \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-2-2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{k} & =2 \\\\ -2 & =2k \\\\ -\\frac{2}{2} & =k \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7ea44ec1-58ba-5956-a980-aec4c772ced8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7ea44ec1-58ba-5956-a980-aec4c772ced8" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ea44ec1-58ba-5956-a980-aec4c772ced8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-864823ca-9fd6-5647-872e-3574bd6be0c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-864823ca-9fd6-5647-872e-3574bd6be0c8" "answer-f712f3e2-029b-5a8a-b19e-340bb36a3186" "answer-d90a60bf-c9df-5642-a65f-043b1fbac549" "answer-332694ea-bd99-5523-b1d8-48a224b3dc34" "answer-6ed8db16-e8bd-5c83-b560-aef74fb47014"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-864823ca-9fd6-5647-872e-3574bd6be0c8" :answer/id #uuid "864823ca-9fd6-5647-872e-3574bd6be0c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f712f3e2-029b-5a8a-b19e-340bb36a3186" :answer/id #uuid "f712f3e2-029b-5a8a-b19e-340bb36a3186" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d90a60bf-c9df-5642-a65f-043b1fbac549" :answer/id #uuid "d90a60bf-c9df-5642-a65f-043b1fbac549" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-332694ea-bd99-5523-b1d8-48a224b3dc34" :answer/id #uuid "332694ea-bd99-5523-b1d8-48a224b3dc34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ed8db16-e8bd-5c83-b560-aef74fb47014" :answer/id #uuid "6ed8db16-e8bd-5c83-b560-aef74fb47014" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060933 :tutorial/content "We can calculate the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ using the following five-step algorithm.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant $\\det(A)$ of the matrix.\n\n**Step 2:** Form the **matrix $M$ of the minors** of $A,$ where each entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ is replaced by its minor $M_{ij}\\mathbin{:}$\n   ![](images/14/14905267240a1e8eb7f54ae47b813c24aa5eb26415c419bbd0ec53425693309b.svg)\n\n**Step 3:** Create the **matrix $C$ of cofactors** by changing the sign of some entries of the matrix of the minors according to the **rule of alternating signs**:\n   \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}+ & - & + \\\\ - & + & - \\\\ + & - & +\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFor each entry of $M$, we change the sign if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$-$\". Otherwise, if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$+$\", then we don't change the entry.\n\nSo, the matrix of cofactors is given by\n\n![](images/a5/a57831b81711ce44dc46c2a3a91b18d8dbfe4078697805369097421351294d2e.svg)\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors, $C^T.$\n\n![](images/e9/e93df3291f387eaac0f6992b38e005f72b08b71b99c7cef8fe6a3b8f42662ebc.svg)\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix:\n   \n\n$$\nA^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{\\det ( A)}C^{T}\n$$\n\nIn other words, we divide each entry of the transpose of the matrix of cofactors by the determinant of the original matrix (which we computed in step 1).\n\nLet's see this in practice, in the next example." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059887 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
